## Preamble

36N9 GENETICS LLC and Michael Laurence Curzi publish the ZXV hardware designs
openly and on purpose, as prior art, so that they stay free of patents for
everyone. Anyone may study, build and improve them for non-commercial
purposes without charge. Anyone who uses these files to manufacture or sell
hardware for commercial purposes agrees, as the price of that permission, to
pay a royalty to the ILLUMAHEART FOUNDATION.

---

## 1. Definitions

**1.1 "Licensor"** means 36N9 GENETICS LLC, PO Box 6, Calpine, CA 96124-0006,
United States, and Michael Laurence Curzi, and their successors and assigns.

**1.2 "Foundation"** means ILLUMAHEART FOUNDATION, an Arizona domestic
nonprofit corporation, Arizona Corporation Commission entity ID 23851761,
known place of business 7220 N 387th Ave, Tonopah, AZ 85354, United States,
or any successor designated under Section 7.4.

**1.3 "Licensed Materials"** means the hardware design files the Licensor
publishes under this Licence, in any form, including schematics, printed
circuit board layouts and fabrication outputs (such as Gerber and drill
files), hardware description language and register-transfer level source
(such as Verilog, SystemVerilog, VHDL, Chisel), netlists, synthesis and
place-and-route scripts, physical layout and mask data (such as GDSII and
OASIS), mechanical and chassis drawings and CAD models, bills of materials,
test vectors, Configuration Files, and their documentation, together with
any Derivative Design.

**1.4 "Configuration Files"** means microcode, firmware images that are part
of the hardware design, FPGA or reconfigurable-fabric bitstreams, hardware
emulation profiles, and any other file that sets or changes the behaviour of
a Product's reconfigurable hardware, including hardware updates and upgrades
the Licensor publishes after a Product is made.

**1.5 "Derivative Design"** means any design, in any form, that is copied
from, adapted from, translated from, or incorporates all or any substantial
part of the Licensed Materials, including a modified, ported, re-targeted,
scaled, re-synthesised or re-laid-out version, and any output a tool
produces from the Licensed Materials.

**1.6 "Licensed Mask Works"** means all mask works and semiconductor
topographies (including registrations under 17 U.S.C. Chapter 9 and
equivalent rights in other countries) owned by the Licensor that are
embodied in the Licensed Materials.

**1.7 "Product"** means any physical article made, in whole or in part,
using the Licensed Materials, a Derivative Design, a Licensed Mask Work, or
Configuration Files, including integrated circuits, dies, chiplets, wafers,
packaged parts, modules, circuit boards, assemblies, chassis, and any device
or system that incorporates any of them, and any reconfigurable device while
it runs Configuration Files.

**1.8 "Commercial Purpose"** means any use intended for or directed toward
commercial advantage or monetary compensation, including manufacturing,
having manufactured, selling, leasing, licensing, offering for sale or
importing a Product; providing a Product, or a service performed using a
Product, to others for a fee; and use of a Product inside a for-profit
organisation in its operations beyond internal evaluation of up to 100
units for up to 12 months.

**1.9 "Noncommercial Purpose"** means any purpose that is not a Commercial
Purpose, including personal study, hobby and private use; teaching and
academic research at an accredited educational institution; research at a
government or public research body; and use by a charitable or nonprofit
organisation for its charitable purpose, in each case without sale of
Products.

**1.10 "Gross Revenue"** means all amounts invoiced, received or receivable,
in cash or in kind, by You and Your Affiliates for the sale, lease, licence
or other disposal of Products, and for services performed using Products,
before any deduction for costs, commissions, taxes or expenses, except
(a) sales, use and value-added taxes separately stated and remitted;
(b) actual credits for returned Products; and (c) separately stated
freight. Non-arm's-length transfers, including to Affiliates, are valued
at the arm's-length price.

**1.11 "Affiliate"** means any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is
under common control with You, where control means ownership of more than
50% of the voting interests or the power to direct management.

**1.12 "Commercial Licence Agreement"** means the agreement in Section 4,
accepted by signature or by the electronic acceptance process the Licensor
provides.

**1.13 "Certification Mark"** means the mark ZXV CERTIFIED and any related
logo, as described in Section 8.

**1.14 "Official Services"** means the update channel through which the
Licensor distributes signed Configuration Files, the device attestation and
key-provisioning service, and any ZXV network, registry or marketplace the
Licensor or the Foundation operates.

**1.15 "You"** means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under
this Licence, and, for the Commercial Licence Agreement, its Affiliates.

**1.16 "Public Infrastructure Use"** means use of a Product by, or supplied
to and used by, a Public Body or a regulated public utility, solely to build,
operate or maintain critical or public infrastructure that serves the public
good, including water and sanitation, energy generation and distribution,
public health and hospitals, emergency and disaster-response services,
public transport, public communications networks, public education, and
environmental monitoring.

**1.17 "Military Use"** means use of a Product, by anyone, in or for
military operations: combat or combat-support operations, weapons,
munitions, weapon targeting, and military intelligence or surveillance
operations. Use by armed forces, defence ministries or their contractors for
non-military purposes, such as administration, logistics, training, health,
engineering, communications or disaster relief outside combat operations,
is not Military Use.

**1.18 "Public Body"** means a national, state, regional or local
government, a government agency, or an intergovernmental organisation, and a nonprofit acting under contract to one of them for that purpose.

