## 2. Defensive Publication

**2.1 Purpose.** The Licensor publishes the Licensed Materials so that they
become prior art. The Licensor does not intend to seek patents on them.

**2.2 Licensor non-assertion.** If the Licensor nonetheless holds or obtains
any patent claim that reads on the Licensed Materials as published, the
Licensor irrevocably agrees not to assert it against anyone who complies
with this Licence.

**2.3 No patents on derivatives by licensees (grant-back).** If You obtain,
or file for, any patent with a claim that reads on a Derivative Design You
made or on the use of the Licensed Materials, You grant the Licensor, the
Foundation and every person licensed under this Licence a worldwide,
royalty-free, non-exclusive, irrevocable licence under that claim, for any
purpose permitted by this Licence.

---

## 3. Open Tier: Noncommercial Licence

**3.1 Grant.** The Licensor grants You a worldwide, royalty-free,
non-exclusive, non-transferable licence, under its copyright and Licensed
Mask Works, to reproduce, study, modify, and create Derivative Designs of
the Licensed Materials; to make, use and give away Products without charge;
and to distribute the Licensed Materials and Derivative Designs under
Section 6; in each case solely for a Noncommercial Purpose.

**3.2 Evaluation by anyone.** Any person, including a for-profit
organisation, may view, study, simulate and internally evaluate the
Licensed Materials, and build up to 10 prototype Products for internal
evaluation that are not sold or used in production, without charge.

**3.3 Perpetual.** The licence in Section 3 is perpetual unless terminated
under Section 9.

**3.4 No commercial rights.** No right is granted under Section 3 for any
Commercial Purpose. Any Commercial Purpose involving the Licensed Materials
or a Product requires the Commercial Licence Agreement. Nothing other than
this Licence or a separate signed agreement gives You permission to copy,
adapt or use the Licensed Materials or Licensed Mask Works for a Commercial
Purpose, and doing so without one infringes the Licensor's rights.

---

## 4. Commercial Licence Agreement (Royalty-Bearing)

**4.1 Acceptance.** You may use the Licensed Materials for a Commercial
Purpose only after accepting this Section 4, by signing it or by completing
the Licensor's electronic acceptance and registration process, which records
Your legal name, address and acceptance date. Acceptance forms a binding
contract between You and the Licensor, for the benefit of the Foundation.

**4.2 Grant.** On acceptance, and conditioned on Your continuing compliance
with Sections 4.3 to 4.7, the Licensor grants You a worldwide,
non-exclusive, non-transferable licence, under its copyright and Licensed
Mask Works, to reproduce and adapt the Licensed Materials and to make, have
made, use, sell, offer for sale, lease, import and otherwise dispose of
Products for any Commercial Purpose, and access to the Official Services for
those Products on the Licensor's published terms.

**4.3 Royalty.** You shall pay a running royalty of **eighteen percent (18%)
of Gross Revenue** from all Products. The royalty is payable directly to the
Foundation, at the payment address or account the Foundation designates in
writing, and is not payable to the Licensor.

**4.4 Payment and reports.** Within 45 days after the end of each calendar
quarter, You shall (a) pay the royalty accrued in that quarter, in United
States dollars, and (b) deliver to the Foundation and the Licensor a report
in the form of Schedule A. Late payments bear interest at 1% per month or
the maximum lawful rate, whichever is lower.

**4.5 Records and audit.** You shall keep complete records supporting each
report for 5 years. The Licensor or the Foundation may, on 30 days'
notice and not more than once per year, have an independent accountant audit
them. If an audit shows an underpayment of more than 5%, You shall pay the
shortfall, interest and the audit cost.

**4.6 Pass-through to contract manufacturers.** If You have Products made by
a third party, You shall bind that party in writing to use the Licensed
Materials only to make Products for You, and You remain liable for royalties
on those Products.

**4.7 Nature of the payment.** Royalty payments are consideration for the
licence in Section 4.2. They are not gifts or charitable contributions by
You.

**4.8 Exhaustion.** Once the royalty has been paid on a Product, that Product
may be resold, used and repaired by any downstream purchaser without further
royalty. Updated Configuration Files the Licensor later publishes may be
installed on a royalty-paid Product without further royalty, subject to the
update terms of the Official Services.

**4.9 Separate agreements.** The Licensor may agree different terms with any
person in a separate signed agreement.

---

## 4A. Public Infrastructure Exemption

**4A.1 Exemption.** No royalty under Section 4.3 is payable on Products, or
on the part of Gross Revenue from Products, that are used solely for Public
Infrastructure Use or for rescue uses under Section 4A.7(a), and never for
any other Military Use. All other terms of this
Licence, including acceptance (4.1), reports (4.4), attribution (Section 6)
and export control (Section 10), still apply.

**4A.2 Conditions.** To rely on the exemption You shall:

(a) register each exempt project with the Licensor before first delivery,
    naming the Public Body or utility, the infrastructure, and the
    approximate number of Products;
(b) report exempt units separately in each quarterly report, with zero
    royalty;
(c) obtain from the Public Body or utility a written statement that the
    Products will be used only for Public Infrastructure Use or rescue
    uses under Section 4A.7(a), and not for any other Military Use, and keep it with Your records under Section 4.5; and
(d) not resell, divert or transfer exempt Products for any other use.

**4A.3 Contractors.** A private company that supplies Products to a Public
Body or utility for Public Infrastructure Use may claim the exemption for
the revenue from that supply only. Its other revenue remains royalty-bearing.

**4A.4 Loss of exemption.** If an exempt Product is used for anything other
than Public Infrastructure Use or rescue uses under Section 4A.7(a), the exemption is lost
for that Product from the start, and the full royalty, with interest under
Section 4.4, becomes due from the party that received the exemption.

**4A.5 Voluntary contributions.** Public Bodies and utilities may still
contribute to the Foundation voluntarily. Such contributions are not
royalties and create no obligation.

**4A.6 Armed forces may use Products for non-military purposes.** Armed
forces and defence ministries may use Products for non-military purposes at
any time, under the same terms as any other user. Such use is not eligible
for the exemption in Section 4A.1 unless it is also Public Infrastructure
Use or a rescue use under Section 4A.7(a).

**4A.7 Military Use is prohibited except in these cases.** No licence is
granted under this Licence, in either tier, for any Military Use except:

(a) **Rescue and life-saving.** Search and rescue, medical evacuation,
    disaster relief, and other missions whose sole purpose is to save human
    life, by any party. These uses qualify for the royalty exemption in
    Section 4A.1 on the same conditions.
(b) **Defence of national sovereignty.** Use by or for a nation, or its
    people, while it is under (i) an actual armed attack by an external
    state or force, or (ii) an armed insurgency within its territory, solely
    to defend itself against that attack or insurgency and only for as long
    as it continues. Use under (b) may include weapons, munitions and weapon
    targeting. These uses are royalty-exempt
    under Section 4A.1.

**4A.8 Limits on defensive use.** Use under Section 4A.7(b):

(a) must comply with international humanitarian law and international human
    rights law;
(b) must not be directed against civilians, peaceful protest, political
    opposition, journalists, or any person not taking direct part in
    hostilities;
(c) does not cover offensive operations beyond what is needed to repel the
    attack or end the insurgency, or the occupation of another state's
    territory; and
(d) ends when the attack or insurgency ends.

An "armed insurgency" means organised armed groups engaged in protracted
armed violence against the state, at the level of a non-international armed
conflict under international humanitarian law. Riots, protests, isolated
violence and political dissent are not an armed insurgency.

**4A.9 Showing a permitted use.** A party relying on Section 4A.7(b) shall,
on request, give the Licensor reasonable evidence of the attack or
insurgency, such as a United Nations Security Council record, a notification
under Article 51 of the United Nations Charter, a recognised declaration of
armed conflict, or an equivalent public record.

**4A.10 Prohibited use terminates.** Any Military Use outside Section 4A.7,
or in breach of Section 4A.8, is unlicensed and terminates all licences of
the party engaged in it, without a cure period.

